---
description: Core rules for the AI Job Application Assistant project
alwaysApply: true
---
- Tech stack is fixed: React+Vite+Tailwind+GSAP frontend, Node+Express+MongoDB backend, JWT auth, Groq for AI, Cloudinary for storage. Do not substitute any of these without asking.
- Only touch files explicitly listed in the module spec pasted into chat. If another file seems needed, ask first instead of guessing.
- Never install a new npm package without naming it and explaining why first.
- Never run git commands without explicit confirmation.
- Never delete or overwrite .env, package.json, or any config file without explicit confirmation.
- Before importing any npm package, verify it's actually listed in package.json — don't assume from memory.
- Keep explanations concise. Don't explain standard code patterns unless asked.
- When a module is complete, summarize what was built and go through its acceptance checklist item by item before stopping.